# Environment variables

Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored — never commit it). Production values go in
Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

```bash
# ── Masumi hosted preprod ──────────────────────────────────────
MASUMI_PAYMENT_BASE_URL=https://<provided-by-organizers>/api/v1
MASUMI_PAYMENT_API_KEY=<read-and-pay key>
MASUMI_REGISTRY_BASE_URL=https://<provided-by-organizers>/api/v1
MASUMI_REGISTRY_API_KEY=<registry key>
MASUMI_NETWORK=Preprod
# V2 source contract address; must match the registered sellers.
MASUMI_SMART_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=addr_test1wzqgalcd93sfjrc5tsc4ycwx80a8lt0s3767a4g8nh45lrg044nd9
MASUMI_SELLING_WALLET_VKEY=<selling wallet vkey>

# Consumer wallet-scoped ReadAndPay key (never Admin).
MASUMI_KEY_CONSUMER=
# Board wallet-scoped ReadAndPay key (never Admin).
MASUMI_KEY_BOARD=
# Board registered seller agent identifier on the V2 source.
MASUMI_AGENT_BOARD=
# Techblog wallet-scoped ReadAndPay key (never Admin).
MASUMI_KEY_TECHBLOG=
# Techblog registered seller agent identifier on the V2 source.
MASUMI_AGENT_TECHBLOG=
# Codepodcast wallet-scoped ReadAndPay key (never Admin).
MASUMI_KEY_CODEPODCAST=
# Codepodcast registered seller agent identifier on the V2 source.
MASUMI_AGENT_CODEPODCAST=
# Devnewsletter wallet-scoped ReadAndPay key (never Admin).
MASUMI_KEY_DEVNEWSLETTER=
# Devnewsletter registered seller agent identifier on the V2 source.
MASUMI_AGENT_DEVNEWSLETTER=
# Gamingforum wallet-scoped ReadAndPay key (never Admin).
MASUMI_KEY_GAMINGFORUM=
# Gamingforum registered seller agent identifier on the V2 source.
MASUMI_AGENT_GAMINGFORUM=

# ── ElevenLabs (CLI + voiceover; project-local, read from env) ──
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ── Models (OpenAI primary, Groq/Gemini LLM fallback) ───────────
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Demo flags ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# false = real Masumi preprod escrows; true = labelled simulated ledger
SIMULATE_PAYMENTS=false
# live = full run; canned = replay of a recorded successful run
DEMO_MODE=live

# ── Board state (Upstash Redis REST) ────────────────────────────
# Unset = in-memory store, fine for `npm run dev`, lost between serverless invocations.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Outcome feed (demo-only signing key for the NeoRack signup feed) ─
# Generate locally: openssl rand -hex 32. Signs simulated signup events.
SHOP_SIGNING_KEY=

# ── Tender Board (demo-only signing key for Board-signed verdicts) ─
# Generate locally: openssl rand -hex 32. Ed25519 key is derived from it.
BOARD_SIGNING_KEY=
```

Rules: keys in Vercel env vars + `.env.local` only — never in the repo,
never in the browser, never on screen. Testnet tx hashes are public and
safe to commit.
